<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Nothing this app stores leaves the device through a backup.

    `android:allowBackup="false"` in the manifest already turns off cloud
    backup. It does not, on Android 12 and up, turn off device-to-device
    transfer — that is what this file is for, and why both sections are here
    rather than only the one that is still doing work.

    The reason is not caution about backups in general. Two things in the app's
    sandbox are decrypted plaintext, deliberately:

      files/pins/…  — attachments the user pinned, written as plaintext so a
                      pin outlives the server-side prune (see lib/pins.ts).
      databases/…   — the local mirror, which is every message body this device
                      has ever decrypted (lib/localdb.ts, opened
                      'no-encryption'). It is what makes search work offline.

    Both are safe where they are: app-private storage, which no other app and no
    media scanner can read. Neither is safe in a Google Drive backup, which is a
    copy held by a third party under a different set of keys — and one nobody
    consented to when they were told the server holds no message bodies.

    The identity seed is unaffected either way: it lives in the Android Keystore
    and is not exportable, so it was never in a backup to begin with. What this
    costs is a restore: a new phone starts at the recovery phrase, which is the
    honest state for an app that has no reset path.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
